\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Class-token latent diagnostics, preliminary study. No world shows collapse by any marginal criterion; on a black background the position is recoverable, and with a per-episode nuisance background it is not. The whitening column matters: on a black background the position lives in low-variance directions, so whitening finds it ($0.71$ px); with the nuisance background whitening does not help, because the information is absent rather than small.}}{19}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
